      "title": "Google DeepMind chief says human-level AI could arrive by 2028",
      "content_html": "Demis Hassabis, co-founder of Google DeepMind, says artificial general intelligence (AGI) could arrive within two to three years, or in 2028 or 2029. In an interview published Oct. 22, the AI researcher said progress in autonomous agents had increased his confidence; his previous estimate was three to five years.\n\nHassabis has described a demanding test for AGI: whether a system could independently derive Albert Einstein’s 1905 physics theories from knowledge available through 1901. He said AI remains years away from meeting that benchmark.",
